CI-repair-09 supplemental evidence packaging

The initial manifest selects the completed first hosted failure and stopped
compiler-expression repair receipts only. It contains no candidate09 native
result and is not the final validation manifest. Add completed native/review/
hosted records explicitly when they exist; never invent a pending pass.

Default operation reads/verifies and prints a proposed immutable index path:

  python3 work/ci-repair-evidence-09/package.py work/ci-repair-evidence-09/manifest-initial.json

Actual publication belongs to the coordinator, under its existing exclusive
claim and after source writers stop. Review the explicit manifest first:

  python3 work/ci-repair-evidence-09/package.py work/ci-repair-evidence-09/manifest-final.json --publish --writers-stopped

The flag records the operator's acknowledgement, not claim acquisition or a
request for new user permission. The helper does not run native tools, Git or
network calls. All final writes are confined to the fixed repository path:
  Documentation/Engineering/Remediation/Evidence/R3/codex-takeover/ci-repair-09/

Never rerun or edit the older package-r3-evidence.py to append these receipts.
Its published08 generated-index.json and receipt objects remain immutable.

Layout and repeat runs
- objects/<sha256>: exact original bytes, deduplicated inside the supplement.
- indexes/<sha256>.json: immutable complete index for this explicit invocation.
- README.md: stable scope explanation; there is no mutable latest index.
- Identical hashes already in prior08 reference that verified prior object.
  Only the pinned prior index and actually reused objects are read; the 22 MB
  historical corpus is neither copied nor scanned in full.
- Same inputs/source/helper produce the same index. New records or changed
  candidate source create a new index without replacing any previous receipt.
- Changed existing objects, symlinks, path traversal, input mutation, missing
  files, hash mismatches and incomplete required receipts produce visible errors.
  A failed publication may leave immutable objects without an index. Do not
  delete/reclaim a lock or reconcile a conflicting receipt automatically.
- Reference the exact printed index in the coordinator's checkpoint. After
  publication, inspect its bytes and hashes before claiming package completeness.

Manifest schema
Top-level schema is swiftj2k-r3-ci-repair-inputs-v1. Unknown top-level fields
are rejected. Paths are absolute or workspace-relative; each input reference is
  {"path": "work/path/to/file.json", "sha256": "64 lowercase hex digits"}
The prior_index path must resolve to the fixed prior08 generated-index.json.
published_base_label is descriptive; the helper does not verify Git identity.
candidate_label is also descriptive, never a qualification result.

Native entries, under native_runs:
  {"result": REF_TO_RESULT_JSON, "command": REF_TO_COMMAND_JSON,
   "before": REF_TO_SOURCE_BEFORE_JSON, "after": REF_TO_SOURCE_AFTER_JSON,
   "reports": [REF_TO_EVERY_XML_UNDER_THIS_RUN], "diagnostic_only": false}

All four files must belong to the same completed run directory. The wrapper's
native.log and exact native.stdout/native.stderr are discovered only through
that directory and their recorded SHA/byte/path metadata. Source before/after
maps and changed_inputs must agree. Ordinary failed exit codes are retained.
Changed source or failed capture requires diagnostic_only=true and is indexed
as such; this is not successful execution evidence. All existing XML must be
explicitly listed. An absent XML framework report is never counted as zero
tests. No declaration/case coverage is inferred by this packager.

Review entries, under reviews:
  {"report": REF, "source": REF, "completed": true, "supporting": [REF, ...]}
Both files are required, the report must be nonempty, and report_sha256 is
checked when present in the source receipt. Explicit active/pending states are
rejected. Completion is the coordinator's explicit attestation; the helper
checks integrity and does not independently approve the review's conclusions.
One-file JSON review receipts may be preserved as explicitly named supplemental
receipts, without pretending they are report/source pairs.

Hosted entries, under hosted_runs:
  {"run_id": 123, "attempt": 1, "metadata": REF_TO_JOBS_JSON,
   "logs": [{"job_id": 456, "file": REF_TO_EXACT_LOG}, ...], "review": REF}
metadata must contain jobs with matching run_id, unique id, status=completed
and an explicit conclusion. Exactly one log must be supplied for every job
in that metadata. Success, failure, cancellation and skipped steps retain their
original meanings. Run attempt and log association are manifest attribution,
not cryptographic provider proof. The separate review receipt must establish
exact PR head/tested checkout/tree, step outcomes, retention and runtime proof.
The packager never upgrades job success into hosted coverage or acceptance.
For first run41186617163, all 32 missing macOS emitter paths are correctly an
incomplete-retention result; there is no successful reconstruction to include.

Additional explicit inputs, under supplemental:
  {"file": REF, "role": "compiler-source-diff"}
Use this for scoped repair before/after files, reports, independent root JSON
reviews, sanitizer inventories/proofs, CI identity reviews and reproduction
helpers. Only receipt/source-text suffixes are allowed; no build trees/binaries.
All references are hashed exactly. No directory glob silently adds evidence.

To append a completed native run, this small coordinator-side pattern creates
the explicit pins (example only; it does not claim any run exists):

  from pathlib import Path
  import hashlib, json
  def ref(p):
      return {"path": str(p.absolute()), "sha256": hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}
  run = Path("work/validation/ACTUAL_COMPLETED_RUN")
  item = {key: ref(run / name) for key, name in (
      ("result", "result.json"), ("command", "command.json"),
      ("before", "source-before.json"), ("after", "source-after.json"))}
  item["reports"] = [ref(p) for p in sorted(run.rglob("*.xml"))]
  manifest["native_runs"].append(item)

Identity and acceptance boundaries
Current Package.swift/Sources/Tests/Scripts contents and modes are captured
separately from .github CI contents/modes. Both are checked again before the
index is written. Documentation and generated evidence are excluded to avoid
self-reference. Native manifests retain their original source identity; a
current-source manifest does not retroactively qualify an earlier test run.

Every index remains NOT_ACCEPTED and explicitly retains UNEXECUTED/UNWAIVED:
combined Part10+15; native3D JPIP; exact WebSocket extension; direct full38 Part2;
multiple transmitted nonempty HT sets. No merge, release or R4 activation follows.

Synthetic verification only:
  python3 work/ci-repair-evidence-09/selftest.py
This creates temporary fake repositories only beneath this work directory,
checks the helper, deletes those fixtures and saves selftest-result.json.
